  "html": "<p class=\"\">In summer 2020 I worked with Carnegie Mellon University's <a href=\"https://delphi.cmu.edu/about/team/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" class=\"external-link group inline-flex items-center text-blue-600 dark:text-blue-400\" data-preview-url=\"https://delphi.cmu.edu/about/team/\">Delphi research group</a> on <a href=\"https://delphi.cmu.edu/epidemic-signals/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" class=\"external-link group inline-flex items-center text-blue-600 dark:text-blue-400\" data-preview-url=\"https://delphi.cmu.edu/epidemic-signals/\">COVIDcast</a>, prototyping data visualizations and interactions to help the public understand hospitalization, transmission and movement trends across the country.</p>\n<p class=\"\">COVIDcast launched in April 2020 with a then-unusual idea: no single signal could be trusted on its own, so it mapped many rough ones side by side. These included doctor and telemedicine visits, symptom searches on Google, flu-test statistics, and symptom surveys run through Facebook and Google. Where several signals agreed, you could believe them.</p>\n<figure role=\"figure\" aria-label=\"Scrolling the COVIDcast dashboard as it runs today — indicator tiles, the county-level map, and the signals table\" class=\"\"><video class=\"img-full my-8 rounded-sm\" autoplay loop muted playsinline preload=\"metadata\" poster=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/ejf/video/upload/so_0,f_jpg,q_auto,w_1280/projects/covidcast/dashboard-scroll.jpg\" src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/ejf/video/upload/q_auto/projects/covidcast/dashboard-scroll.mp4\" aria-label=\"Scrolling the COVIDcast dashboard as it runs today — indicator tiles, the county-level map, and the signals table\"></video><figcaption class=\"\">Scrolling the COVIDcast dashboard as it runs today — indicator tiles, the county-level map, and the signals table</figcaption></figure>\n<figure role=\"figure\" aria-label=\"COVIDcast dashboard: weekly case, hospitalization, and death rates above an interactive county-level map\" class=\"\">\n<img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/ejf/image/upload/c_scale,f_auto,q_auto:good,w_1280/v1666630395/project-images/cmu_covidcast.png\" alt=\"COVIDcast dashboard: weekly case, hospitalization, and death rates above an interactive county-level map\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" srcset=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/ejf/image/upload/c_scale,f_auto,q_auto:good,w_640/v1666630395/project-images/cmu_covidcast.png 640w, https://res.cloudinary.com/ejf/image/upload/c_scale,f_auto,q_auto:good,w_960/v1666630395/project-images/cmu_covidcast.png 960w, https://res.cloudinary.com/ejf/image/upload/c_scale,f_auto,q_auto:good,w_1280/v1666630395/project-images/cmu_covidcast.png 1280w, https://res.cloudinary.com/ejf/image/upload/c_scale,f_auto,q_auto:good,w_1920/v1666630395/project-images/cmu_covidcast.png 1920w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 430px) 92vw, (max-width: 768px) 85vw, 900px\" title=\"COVIDcast dashboard: weekly case, hospitalization, and death rates above an interactive county-level map\" width=\"5001\" height=\"2625\" data-dimensions=\"5001×2625\" class=\"img-full my-8 rounded-sm w-full mx-auto py-4\" crossorigin=\"anonymous\">\n<figcaption class=\"\">COVIDcast dashboard: weekly case, hospitalization, and death rates above an interactive county-level map</figcaption>\n</figure>\n<p class=\"\">I kept playing with the data afterwards. Using Delphi's open Epidata API, I made time-lapses of doctor visits by county, where each circle is a county sized by the share of outpatient visits due to COVID-like symptoms. One was paired with a data sonification of the same numbers for all of New York State.</p>\n<figure role=\"figure\" aria-label=\"A county-level circle map of the United States, one circle per county\" class=\"\">\n<img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/ejf/image/upload/c_scale,f_auto,q_auto:good,w_1280/v1755099710/screenshot_2025-08-13_at_11.41.38_AM.png\" alt=\"A county-level circle map of the United States, one circle per county\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" srcset=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/ejf/image/upload/c_scale,f_auto,q_auto:good,w_640/v1755099710/screenshot_2025-08-13_at_11.41.38_AM.png 640w, https://res.cloudinary.com/ejf/image/upload/c_scale,f_auto,q_auto:good,w_960/v1755099710/screenshot_2025-08-13_at_11.41.38_AM.png 960w, https://res.cloudinary.com/ejf/image/upload/c_scale,f_auto,q_auto:good,w_1280/v1755099710/screenshot_2025-08-13_at_11.41.38_AM.png 1280w, https://res.cloudinary.com/ejf/image/upload/c_scale,f_auto,q_auto:good,w_1920/v1755099710/screenshot_2025-08-13_at_11.41.38_AM.png 1920w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 430px) 92vw, (max-width: 768px) 85vw, 900px\" title=\"A county-level circle map of the United States, one circle per county\" width=\"1576\" height=\"1110\" data-dimensions=\"1576×1110\" class=\"img-full my-8 rounded-sm w-full mx-auto py-4\" crossorigin=\"anonymous\">\n<figcaption class=\"\">A county-level circle map of the United States, one circle per county</figcaption>\n</figure>",
